PROBLEM 3.1:-
At first  I was confused between bubble sort, selection sort and insertion sort because all three were doing sorting in different ways. I understood that bubble sort compares nearby elements and swaps them, selection sort finds the smallest element and puts it in the correct place, and insertion sort takes one element and puts it in its correct position. I learned that if the array is already sorted, insertion sort can be faster because it does not need to do unnecessary swapping.

